CLARIFICATION ON MY OWN DoD 2, from the row that filed this one. I wrote "passes UNCHANGED"; that is one word too strong and I am fixing it here rather than leaving a contradiction for the worker.

`tests/e2e/control-room/activation-fresh-project.spec.ts` lands PARKED. Its first statement is:

```ts
test.fixme(true, "blocked on task-d342a2b158764fefa8dbf2a5365e7bf7: the browser activation chain never installs the policy, so project.activate refuses ACTIVATION_POLICY_UNMEASURED");
```

DELETING THAT ONE LINE IS THE WHOLE OF THE RE-ENABLE, and it is expected work for this row. Nothing else in the spec may change. Read DoD 2 as: every assertion below that line passes with no assertion relaxed, no timeout inflated, no `toContain` softened to a truthiness check, and no arm deleted.

WHY IT IS PARKED RATHER THAN LEFT RED: the branch is shared, and a knowingly-red lane costs every other row a false attribution — a peer running `pnpm test:e2e:browser` would find a failure that is neither theirs nor news. It is `fixme` rather than `skip` so the reason travels with it in the runner output.

WHAT THE SPEC ALREADY PROVES, verified live before it was parked — the failure is the LAST step, not the first, and everything ahead of it is real evidence you can rely on while fixing:
- `lane.seedPid` is null, so the store was never seeded;
- a real pairing handshake completes (`operatorChannel: true`, the label read from the page and typed back on the daemon's own channel — `liveCredentials: "ATTACHED"` alone does NOT pair the tab, the app refuses with "Moe was started without a terminal it can listen on");
- `cr.activate.root` mounts with `cr.activate.refusal` absent, so `/activation/read` answered with receipts;
- `cr.activate.reason.repository` contains the lane's real `git rev-parse HEAD`, and no receipt row reads as a `<projectId>-*` placeholder;
- a pre-activation `goal.create_with_source` is REFUSED and the refusal text is the copy task-ac9d5e2d rewrote (asserted not to contain the old terminal-bound sentence);
- `project.register`, `project.bind_repository` and `provider.probe` all reach `data-ok="true"`.

Only `cr.activate.step.project.activate` is `data-ok="false"`. That is your one target.

TWO LANE FACTS THAT COST ME ROUND TRIPS, so they do not cost you any:
- `cr.goals.newgoal.prd.input` is a `type="file"` input (new-goal-form.tsx:130), so it needs `setInputFiles({buffer, mimeType, name})`, not `.fill()`. Without a real attachment the browser sends brief-only `goal.create`, a different kind than DoD 1 asks for.
- `cr.goals.newgoal.prd.status` states the sha256 the BROWSER computed, not the filename — assert the digest.
- The accepted create renders `Goal created: <title>` (live-goal-create.ts:131), never the wire's enums.

Also note for whoever plans this: `pnpm test:e2e:browser -- <name>` does NOT filter; it runs the whole lane. Use `npx playwright test -c tests/e2e/control-room/playwright.config.ts <name>`.
